WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.469
-Now, I did not know this.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
Beanie, a name given to you
by your nanny.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that correct?
-Yes.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How´d it come about?
-I had a nanny when I young.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.809
My mom was working.
And my given name is Elizabeth.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.244
And she called me Elizabeanie,

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause that´s a popular
British nickname.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.781
-Oh, okay.
-And my brothers are much older.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:15.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´re like,
"Let´s just call her Beanie.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s so funny."
And it totally stuck.

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.854
-So you had no decision in this
at all?

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.689
-No, but everyone was like,

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
"At 10,
you´ll want to be Elizabeth.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
At 16" --
Everyone had a different age.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:27.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were like,
"You´re gonna outgrow it."

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "No."
I love it.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, good.
Well, that works out good.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.032
So, your brother is Jonah Hill?

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And he has been here before

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:36.669
and talked about your mother
being a very funny character.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-A wonderful mother as well.

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you stayed with her
recently.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.675
She made you stay with her while
you were shooting this film.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:45.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
Sharon, Shea, as we call her.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:46.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
She´s the best.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:47.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The nanny --
Did the nanny give her Shea?

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I did.
-Okay.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
She´s truly the best woman
on planet Earth.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.520 size:81% position:41%
But she´s a character.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.356
And I was basically told
the day I stay in a hotel

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:59.025
over staying with her would be
like the worst day of her life.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So when we were filming
"Lady Bird,"

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.730
I was staying with my parents.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:08.234 size:84% position:42%
And I came home one day
and she was <i>geschreing,</i>

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is Yiddish for, like,
screaming her face off.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
-Turning purple, like --

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I hear it, and I´m, like,
running into her office,

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:18.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she´s, like,
screaming on the phone.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:22.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
She´s like,
"I am my dog´s advocate!

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:23.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay?"

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
She´s --
I´m like, "What´s going on?"

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
I realize
she´s talking to the vet.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And she´s like --

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:30.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
She´s like,
"My dog can´t speak English!

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:35.195
My dog can´t tell you when
he´s upset, so I speak for him."

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
She´s screaming.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´m like,
"What is going on?"

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
She hangs up.
I´m like, "What´s going on?"

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
She´s like,
"I´m mad at the vet."

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.037
And just, like, walks out of
the room. I´m like, "What?"

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:47.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
The next day, my parents get
a registered letter,

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:49.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is like one step
under getting served, right?

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, it´s basically
getting served.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:54.714
-In this day,
if it´s too much for an e-mail,

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
that´s a huge deal.
-Exactly.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:59.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You have to sign for it, okay?

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:02.655
So they get a registered letter
to our house

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.658
that says in not so many words

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:08.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
that my parents are never
welcome at the vet ever again.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we have the letter --
and this is my favorite thing,

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:12.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause it´s so clearly
from the vet,

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.167
´cause at the end it says,

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
"If your next veterinarian has
any questions

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.871
regarding Brewski´s care."

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:20.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"Please" --

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.509
-"You have made it impossible

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:25.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the doctors and staff here
to communicate with you."

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s the best.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, also, like,
I have to assume

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
the vet doesn´t know
how to do that.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like they talk
and they´re like,

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:32.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What should we do?"
And they´re like,

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.154
"I think there´s a thing, like,
in the legal profession

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you send
a registered letter?"

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.891 size:84% position:42%
-Exactly. "I think that
we´re able to do that."

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Oh, my God.
That´s really, really great.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this -- tell us about
the part you play.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:45.131
Because you are -- you´re
a student in a Catholic school.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
As we can tell from the clip.
-Yes. Yes.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you have any background
in that?

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:50.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Certainly not.
Feldstein -- quite Jewish.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, right.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, <i>geschreing </i>didn´t
seem like something

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:56.309 size:75% position:38%
that you heard a lot
in Catholic schools.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:59.946
-Exactly. And it was amazing,
because I learned so much.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
Saoirse, she´s not American,
but she is Catholic.

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.117
Or she was raised Catholic.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so she was teaching me
the Hail Mary

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.221
and I was teaching her
the pledge of allegiance.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:09.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, perfect.
-Because we had, like,

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:11.658
all of these classroom scenes

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we had to do
both of those things.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.527 size:84% position:42%
And I was like, "Okay,
´I pledge allegiance.´"

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:15.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was like, "Hail Mary,
full of grace."

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:17.130
I was like, "Okay, okay."

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.432
Sort of feeding each other lines
back and forth. Yeah.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And what drew you to the part
you play in this?

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:23.236
-I love this movie so much.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
Greta Gerwig is a genius.
-She´s wonderful.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And she wrote
the most amazing script.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it said --
when I got the script,

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:32.011
it said Julie, 17, chubby,

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
gets the lead
in her high school musical.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:36.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Excuse me?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:38.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Sounds great."

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:41.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just felt like
such a perfect fit.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.823
And the story of a young girl.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just don´t have
enough of these

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
complicated female roles
and female movies

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
and specifically Julie
just, like,

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
felt like a very good fit
for me.

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you´re on Broadway
right now.

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´re doing "Hello, Dolly!"
with Bette Midler.

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:56.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
You also --
You went to theater camp.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
You knew you wanted to do this
for a long time.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:58.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-What´s it called, Stagedoor?

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Stagedoor Manor.
-Stagedoor Manor.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you -- Is that where
you meet Ben Platt?

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:03.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s not where
I met Ben Platt.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:04.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ben and I have been
best friends --

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
We met at a bat mitzvah,
actually.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:11.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course.
-A Catholic bat mitzvah?

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, of course.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:15.221 size:88% position:44%
I was wearing my uniform
that I wear in the film.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
It would be really funny

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
to do a Catholic-themed
bat mitzvah.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:21.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-I´m in. I´m so in.

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, of course,
Ben and I both had, like,

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
theater-themed bar mitzvah
and bat mitzvahs.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-But we met at a bat mitzvah,

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.834
and this was before cellphones.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:30.003
So we didn´t have any way
to, like, stay in touch.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.471
He joined my school in 9th grade

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we instantly became
best friends.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:36.376
And sort of the way that, like,
he knew we were best friends

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:38.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
was like the second
week of school.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:41.047 size:84% position:42%
He got his braces off
and he texted me, like,

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.282 size:81% position:41%
"I got my braces off."

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:45.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I left my class
to come see his teeth.

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:47.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:49.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´m such a goodie-goodie
and I love school.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he was like,
"I must mean a lot to you

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you left
to see my teeth."

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:55.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What did the teacher say
when you just got up and left?

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.230
-I mean, I think I was like,
"I have to pee," or something.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I played it off, Seth.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously I played it off.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
Good, because you´re so
successfully now,

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.703
I can´t believe you just would
have burned down high school

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.338 size:84% position:42%
to see a pair of teeth.

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:06.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:07.840 size:78% position:39%
Congrats on the film.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my gosh, I´m so honored.
Truly.

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Such a pleasure
to have you here.

